-- title:
--   Geometric fibres of the level-(n;ℓ) uniformisation
-- statement:
--   The theorem is a statement about the fibres, over algebraically closed fields, of a formal uniformisation map at level $(n;\ell)$ for the Čerednik–Drinfeld situation. Its data and hypotheses are the following.
--
--   Numerical data. Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$, subject to $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), $r\nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r\nmid N$ (`hrbarN`), and $N$ squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   Base rings. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adic completeness of $\mathcal O$ (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/\pi$ of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   The unramified layer. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, and the hypotheses: $Onr$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies, modulo $\pi$, a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   The determinant valuation. A homomorphism $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ holds exactly when $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   The indefinite quaternion side and the coarse space. Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ is ramified in $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ exactly when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point rule `pt` assigning to each fake elliptic curve over an $\mathcal O$-scheme-point a section, such that `h𝒳` holds: `pt` is invariant under isomorphism, compatible with pullback, bijective on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and universal among such rules.
--
--   Level $n$ and the twisting group. A natural number $n$ with $3\le n$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule `ptF` on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure satisfying the fine moduli axioms `hM` (isomorphism invariance, pullback compatibility, surjectivity and injectivity of the point rule on all affine bases); a group $G$ with a homomorphism $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `hρ`, i.e. $\rho$ acts over the base, realises level twisting by $\chi(h)$ on point rules, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, unital, surjective and injective modulo $n$.
--
--   Forgetting the level. A morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and compatible with the two point rules (`hp_pt`).
--
--   The Hecke data away from $r,\bar r$. For each prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule `ptT` on curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure satisfying the coarse axioms `h𝒴`, and two degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell):\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points are forgetting the extra structure (`hd₀`) and passing to an $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`).
--
--   Atkin–Lehner involutions. Morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $r$ (`har`) and at $\bar r$ (`harbar`).
--
--   The definite quaternion side. Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and the finite ramification locus is exactly the place over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$ (`hv`).
--
--   The discrete groups. A subgroup $\Gamma t$ of the unit group of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$, characterised (`hΓt`) as the group of units lying in the local box subgroup of $R_1$ at every place different from $v$; for each admissible $\ell$, elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ with `hs` (four clauses per $\ell$): $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at all places not over $r$, component $1$ at places over $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; and $\Gamma t_\ell=\Gamma t\cap s_\ell\Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   Integral coordinates. All rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and a map $coord:\Lambda\to Zp2_r\times Zp2_r$ satisfying `hcoord`: additivity, the normalisation $coord(1)=(1,0)$, the $\varpi$-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace condition.
--
--   The curve over the residue field and its formal module. A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over $Onr/\pi$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), two-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀`: $A_0$ is a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$.
--
--   The $\Gamma t$-action on $A_0$ by quasi-isogenies. Families $e,e':\Gamma t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg$, together with: `hE1` each pair $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure; `hE1mul` multiplicativity up to multiplication by powers of $r$; `hE1sc` rational scalars $\gamma$ give scalar $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; `hE1'` conversely, if $e\gamma$ becomes a scalar up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar; `hE2` for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is computed on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; `hE3` the level-$n$ structure $P_0$ is moved by $e\gamma$ by a label $lab(\gamma)\in\Lambda$, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$; `hE4` over an algebraically closed field, every level-preserving self-isogeny of degree a power of $r$ of a pullback of $A_0$ agrees, up to powers of $r$, with some $e\gamma$.
--
--   The Eichler and twin orders acting on $A_0$. An order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators relative to $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), a family $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`), and the hypotheses `hE5a` (each $\hat e(x)$ is a homomorphism for the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unit, multiplicativity, and agreement with the $\Lambda$-action on integers), `hE5c` ($\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (agreement with $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$ when $x=r^k\gamma$), `hE5e` (the joint formal-coordinate normalisation for $e$ and $\hat e$ with one and the same $g$), `hE5g` ($R_2$ is stable under the main involution). A second maximal order $\Lambda_{1s}$ (`hΛ₁s`) containing $R_1$ (`hR₁Λ₁s`) with $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$ (`htwin`); an order $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ (`hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`) with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂'r`) containing $R_2$ (`hR₂R₂'`), a family $\hat e':R_2'\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê'`), and the hypotheses `hE6a` (group-law homomorphism and commutation with $\Lambda$), `hE6b1`–`hE6b3`, `hE6c`, `hE6d` (restriction to $R_2$ is $\hat e$), `hE6e1` (stability under the involution), `hE6e2` (injectivity of $\hat e'$) and `hE6f` (if $\hat e'(z)$ kills all $q$-torsion for a prime $q\neq r$, then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_{1s}$ for some $K$).
--
--   The formal moduli package. A ring map $\iota:Zp2_r\to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a rule $\eta$ sending rigidified objects over $Onr$-algebras with $r$ nilpotent to $MD$-points, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible rigidifications $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every $MD$-point is locally of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$); an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image has a uniform $r$-power denominator with respect to $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   The Drinfeld comparison. A family of maps $eD$ from the $MD$-point functor over $\mathcal O$ to the product of the functor $B\mapsto\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(Onr,B)$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$, for Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, subject to: naturality (`hnatD`), bijectivity (`hbijD`), compatibility with the leg $\psi$ in the first coordinate (`hfstD`), translation of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action into the twisted action on pairs (`hGLD`), the effect of a $\pi$-translate on the leg with the Deligne datum unchanged (`hPiD`), and existence of $\pi$-translates (`hPiexD`).
--
--   Comparison of the two reductions. A ring map $\kappa:Onr/\pi\to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   Atkin–Lehner data on $A_0$ at $\bar r$. A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ over the base and an integer $k_w$ such that $(a_w,a_w')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving the level (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`: the formal-coordinate normalisation holds simultaneously for all $e\gamma$ and for $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, the latter matching $r^{k}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   The comparison functor $\Xi$. For each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a leg $\psi:Onr\to B$ and a rigidified curve over $B$, a point $\Xi$ of the $MD$-point functor, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality along pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves compatible up to powers of $r$), and `hΞdef` (the explicit description of $\Xi$ through $\eta$, a transported rigidification with $j\le 1$ and admissibility for the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$).
--
--   Equivariance. An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and the three clauses `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`: translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$, by the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$, or by an $\ell$-level isogeny matching the adelic data of `hs` and the joint normalisation, corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\,\cdot\,)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some integer $c$, with $\,\cdot\,$ equal to $\gamma$, to $\bar w$, and to $\ell s^{-1}$ respectively.
--
--   The level-$n$ uniformisation. A monoid homomorphism $\theta t:\Gamma t\to G$ and a family of maps $\Theta f$ from the product functor $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(Onr,-)\times\Omega_{K_0,\pi}\times G$ to the nilpotent points of $f_M$, subject to naturality (`hnat`), $G$-equivariance (`hG`), invariance under the twisted $\Gamma t$-action (`hi'`), a unique-lifting property along suitable surjections (`het`), and the fibre criterion `hfib` over algebraically closed fields.
--
--   The transport clauses. `hC0e` and `hC0u`: existence and uniqueness of the norm-level transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification. `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`: existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism of rigidified curves, and pullback, of a rigidified curve matching a given pair $(\psi,P)$ under $eD$ and $g_0^{-1}$. `hC2` and `hC2c`: the first component of $\Theta f((\psi,P),1)$ is the level-$n$ point of the matching curve with its transported level structure, and composing it with $p$ gives the coarse point of the curve. `hC3`: translating $(\psi,P)$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma t$ produces a second rigidification of the same curve, matching the translated pair, whose transported level-$n$ structure is the $\chi(\theta t\gamma)$-twist of the first, and whose extra level-$\ell'$ structures (for primes $\ell'\neq r$ invertible in the base) agree whenever both are compatible with a given extra level structure on $A_0$. `hC4` and `hC4pi`: the analogous statements for the action of $r^{c}g_0\iota_0(h)g_0^{-1}$ and for $\pi$-translates. `hC5`: over an algebraically closed field, an isomorphism between two curves matching $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$, both rigidified over one and the same leg, yields $\gamma\in\Gamma t$ with $(\psi,P')$ the twisted translate of $(\psi,P)$ by $\iota_0(\gamma)$, with the isomorphism carrying the $\chi(\theta t\gamma)$-twist of the transported level-$n$ structure to the other one, and with the extra level-$\ell'$ structures matching under the isomorphism precisely when the corresponding extra level structure on $A_0$ is stable under $e\gamma$.
--
--   The extra level $\ell$ on $A_0$. For each admissible $\ell$, an extra level-$\ell$ structure $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$, a curve $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with morphisms $as,as',bs,bs'$ and integers $ks(\ell)$ such that $(as,as')$ realises the $\ell$-level isogeny of $(A_0,C_0(\ell))$ (`hLIs`), $(bs,bs')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{ks(\ell)}$ (`hBSs`) preserving the level (`hBSslev`), and `hJOINTs` is the joint formal-coordinate normalisation for the $e\gamma$ together with $as$ followed by $bs$, the latter matching $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$. The stabiliser dictionary `hSTAB`: $e\gamma$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ if and only if $\gamma\in\Gamma t_\ell$. The clauses `hCLe` and `hCLu`: existence and essential uniqueness of an extra level-$\ell'$ structure on a rigidified curve compatible with a given one on $A_0$. A family of maps $\Theta T$ to the nilpotent points of $g_\ell$, natural (`hnatT`), whose value at a matching pair is the $\ell$-coarse point of the curve with its extra structure (`hVT`).
--
--   The fixed prime and the level-$(n;\ell)$ space. A prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$; a scheme $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule $ptF_\ell$ on triples (curve, full level $n$, extra level $\ell$) satisfying the fine moduli axioms `hMℓ`; morphisms $\pi_\ell:M_\ell\to M$ and $p_\ell:M_\ell\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base (`hπℓf`, `hpℓg`) compatible with the point rules (`hπℓ`, `hpℓ`); an action $\rho_\ell$ of $G$ on $M_\ell$ over the base (`hρℓf`) commuting with $\pi_\ell$ (`hρℓπ`), fixing $p_\ell$ (`hρℓp`), and realising twisting by $\chi(h)$ on $ptF_\ell$ when the extra structures match (`hρℓtw`).
--
--   Finally, a family of maps $\Theta f_\ell$ from $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(Onr,-)\times\Omega_{K_0,\pi}\times G$ to the nilpotent points of $f_{M_\ell}$, natural in the base (`hnatℓ`), $G$-equivariant (`hGℓ`), with value $\Theta f_\ell((\psi,P),1)$ equal to the level-$(n;\ell)$ point of the matching curve with its transported level-$n$ structure and an extra level-$\ell$ structure compatible with $C_0(\ell)$ (`hVALℓ`), and invariant under the twisted action of elements of $\Gamma t$ lying in $\Gamma t_\ell$ (`hiℓ`).
--
--   Conclusion. For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, for all $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi,\psi':Onr\to k$, all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$, and all $g,g'\in G$, the equality
--   $$\Theta f_\ell\bigl((\psi,P),g\bigr)=\Theta f_\ell\bigl((\psi',P'),g'\bigr)$$
--   holds if and only if there exists a unit $\gamma$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma t$ such that all of the following hold:
--
--   (i) $\gamma\in\Gamma t_\ell$, that is, $\gamma\in\Gamma t\cap s_\ell\Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$;
--
--   (ii) $g'=\theta t(\gamma)\,g$;
--
--   (iii) $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`: for every full lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$, the line of $P'$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed comparison isomorphism;
--
--   (iv) for every $y\in Onr$, if $y$ is fixed by $Fr^{\,vdet(\iota_0(z))}$ for every $z\in\Gamma t$ which is a rational scalar and satisfies $\theta t(z)=1$, then $\psi'(y)=\psi\bigl(Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0(\gamma))}(y)\bigr)$, where $vdet(\iota_0(\cdot))$ is read as an integer.
--
--   Thus the conclusion is the level-$(n;\ell)$ analogue of the hypothesis `hfib`, with the single additional conjunct (i) on $\gamma$.
--
--   This is the fibre computation underlying Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at level $(n;\ell)$: it says that the formal uniformisation map $\Theta f_\ell$ identifies two triples (leg, Deligne datum, group element) exactly when they differ by an element of $\Gamma t\cap s_\ell\Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$, so that the geometric fibres of the level-$(n;\ell)$ family are orbits of that smaller discrete group. It is the version in which the curve-isomorphism clause `hC5` is formulated over a single leg, and it is used by the statement that combines the fibre description with the translation action on the level-$(n;\ell)$ family over Noetherian bases.
